{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And each man shall be.</b> Every one of the officers of Hezekiah, or he himself." "<b>Like a hiding place from wind.</b> A place, and it is a verb from the heavy [causative] binyan added [i.e., the hif'il]." "Like ציון, from the root ציה, like חורב (1 Kings 18)." "<b>In a weary land.</b> Thirsty, like 'in a weary land for you' (Psalms 103:1)." "[And the meaning of] <b>And each man shall be.</b> Judah, like one sitting in a place of hiding from wind."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {3 "Psalms 63:2 is the verse that contains the phrase 'in a weary land'; Ibn Ezra cites it as קמ\"ג (143), which is a misnumbering. The verse reads 'צמאה לך נפשי' (Psalms 63:2)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:17.665811044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}